num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX045\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States 'The US withholds **15%** on US dividends paid to an Irish UCITS ETF. That is the US–Ireland treaty rate', matching the source.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says the tax is 'levied on the fund' and 'withheld before dividends reach the fund', reducing distributions or NAV. Also says 'Investors generally cannot reclaim or credit the 15%'. This covers both the fund bearing the cost and investors' inability to reclaim. Saying investors bear it 'economically' through NAV is consistent with the fund bearing it.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required minimums are fully covered: 15% treaty withholding, and a fund-level cost that investors cannot reclaim. There is no zero-rate claim and no claim that investors can reclaim directly. The side claims (MSCI net index assumption, gross roll-up, 871(m) and level-1 framing) are outside scope and not contradicted by the evidence. The answer is truncated at the end, but nothing false is asserted.\"}","ttft_ms":4925,"type":"result","duration_ms":8276,"uuid":"74be9eac-020b-4187-a486-49cbcb381044","ttft_stream_ms":647,"time_to_request_ms":76,"first_content_frame_ms":647,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
